## Concordant measures (upper-half inequality rose)
SD up; P75, P90, P99 up strongly in dollars; IQR up (+40 to +62%); P90-P50 up; P90/P50 nearly
tripled for both sexes; Gini(trunc) up modestly for both; share at or below zero jumped 16-19 pp.

## Discordant measures
P50 fell (-43% M, -56% F) while upper percentiles rose; top-1% share FELL ~4-5 pp; the
positive-subsample Gini FELL 7-8 pp (conditional on holding positive wealth, the positive
distribution flattened, partly composition: the positive subsample in 1996 includes many
low-wealth people previously at/below the zero mass).

## Jail strata (descriptive only; no inference)
- White males ever_jailed=1 (N=57): levels far lower (mean ~26k vs ~89k; P50 1,400 -> 0);
  share<=0 38.6% -> 56.1%; Gini(trunc) ~0.86-0.87, higher than non-jailed (~0.78-0.79).
- White females ever_jailed=1 (N=12): tiny cell; mean 2,718 -> 6,435; two-thirds or more at or
  below zero in both years; all dispersion figures unstable, none usable for inference.

## Sensitivity to full-row duplicates
Dropping exact duplicate rows (WM 648, WF 516 dropped, mostly zero/low-wealth ties) lowers
levels of SD/IQR/top shares but preserves the DIRECTION of change for IQR (up), P90-P50 (up),
Gini(trunc) (up ~1.2-1.7 pp), top10 share (flat). The P50 decline is NOT robust: deduplicated
P50 rises 31,600 -> 37,100 for males and is flat (37,450 -> 37,054) for females. The median
result is an artefact of differential duplication of zero-wealth rows and should not be leaned on.

## Caveats
Nominal dollars (deflation would modestly shrink increases); no respondent ID, so cross-sectional
comparison only; ever_jailed = jailed 1985-1994 fixed label; small jail cells; extreme tails make
SD sensitive; ratios undefined because P10=P25=0.
